---
/**
 * Art. 13 privacy notice for accommodation guests (English).
 *
 * Deliberately unlisted: noindex, absent from nav, footer and sitemap, linked
 * only from the check-in form. Art. 13 requires the information to reach the
 * data subject at the point of collection — it does not require the page to be
 * publicly discoverable, and the website privacy policy covers a different
 * audience, purpose and legal basis entirely.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const h2 = 'font-subtitle text-[clamp(24px,2.4vw,32px)] text-warm-dark mt-12 mb-4';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Guest Privacy Notice — Laitse Castle"
  description="How Nevaliste OÜ processes accommodation guests' data under § 24 of the Estonian Tourism Act."
  locale="en"
  noAnalytics={true}
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-prose mx-auto">
      <p class="font-ui uppercase tracking-wider text-[15px] font-bold text-burgundy mb-5">Accommodation</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(30px,6vw,58px)] leading-[1.05] tracking-display text-warm-dark mb-8">
        Guest privacy notice
      </h1>

      <div class="font-body text-body-lg text-warm-dark leading-relaxed space-y-6">
        <p>
          This notice explains how we handle your data when you stay overnight at Laitse
          Castle. Website visits, cookies and analytics are covered separately by our
          <a href="/en/privacy-policy" class="text-burgundy font-bold underline underline-offset-4">website privacy policy</a> —
          that is a different processing activity resting on a different legal basis.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Data controller</h2>
        <p>
          Nevaliste OÜ, Lossi tee 9, 76302 Laitse, Harju County, Estonia.
          <a href="mailto:info@laitsecastle.ee" class="text-burgundy font-bold underline underline-offset-4">info@laitsecastle.ee</a>,
          tel <a href="tel:+37254210881" class="text-burgundy font-bold underline underline-offset-4">+372 5421 0881</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Why we collect this</h2>
        <p>
          As an accommodation provider we are required to register every guest before their
          stay begins. The obligation comes from
          <strong class="font-bold"> § 24 of the Estonian Tourism Act</strong> (turismiseadus).
        </p>
        <p>
          The legal basis is <strong class="font-bold">compliance with a legal obligation</strong> —
          GDPR Art. 6(1)(c). It is not based on consent, so it cannot be withdrawn.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>What we collect</h2>
        <p>From every adult guest (§ 24(2)):</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>given and family name(s);</li>
          <li>date of birth;</li>
          <li>citizenship;</li>
          <li>country of residence — <em>country only, not a street address</em>;</li>
          <li>dates of stay;</li>
          <li>reason for the stay;</li>
          <li>number of accompanying children under 18.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We ask for travel document type, number and issuing country only if you are
          <strong class="font-bold">neither an EEA nor a Swiss citizen and your country of
          residence is not Estonia</strong> (§ 24(3)). No other guest is asked for these
          details or has them stored — including third-country nationals living in
          Estonia, whom the law exempts (§ 24(2)).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="font-bold">No data is collected about the children themselves</strong> —
          only how many are staying with you (§ 24(4)).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="font-bold">We do not store a photo or copy of your identity
          document.</strong> The law provides for registration <em>on the basis of</em>
          the document, not for retaining an image of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="font-bold">Phone and email.</strong> These are not required by law —
          we ask only so we can reach you about your stay. They rest on the accommodation
          contract and are deleted after six months.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Do you have to provide it?</h2>
        <p>
          Yes. Providing the details above is a <strong class="font-bold">statutory
          requirement</strong>, and we cannot accommodate you without them. Providing a
          phone number and email is not a statutory requirement.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          Under § 24(8) of the Tourism Act we are obliged to disclose this data on request
          to the <strong class="font-bold">Police and Border Guard Board</strong> and to
          security authorities. We do not share or sell it otherwise.
        </p>
        <p>
          The data is held in a Supabase database on servers in the European Union.
          Supabase acts as our processor. Nothing is transferred outside the EEA.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          <strong class="font-bold">Two years</strong> from the date of registration, as
          required by § 24(7) of the Tourism Act. This is not our choice — the law obliges
          us to retain it for that period. After two years it is deleted automatically.
        </p>
        <p>Phone and email are deleted after six months.</p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You may access your data, require inaccurate details to be corrected, restrict
          processing, and object to processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="font-bold">Exception regarding erasure.</strong> Because we process
          this data to comply with a legal obligation, we cannot erase it on request during
          the two-year period — GDPR Art. 17(3)(b) removes the right to erasure where
          processing is required by law. All your other rights apply in full. Phone and
          email, which the law does not require, we will delete at any time on request.
        </p>
        <p>
          No automated decision-making or profiling is carried out on your data.
        </p>

        <h2 class={h2}>Questions and complaints</h2>
        <p>
          Write to
          <a href="mailto:info@laitsecastle.ee" class="text-burgundy font-bold underline underline-offset-4">info@laitsecastle.ee</a>.
          You may also lodge a complaint with the Estonian Data Protection Inspectorate
          (<a href="https://www.aki.ee" class="text-burgundy font-bold underline underline-offset-4" rel="noopener">aki.ee</a>).
        </p>

        <p class="pt-6">
          <a href="/en/check-in" class="text-burgundy font-bold underline underline-offset-4">← Back to the check-in form</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
